---
title: Nashville hot potatoes
tags: [american]
cuisine: american
source: Nashville hot potatoes by StarChefs, https://www.starchefs.com/recipes/nashville-hot-potatoes
---

> A restaurant batch: the spice mix, ranch and potatoes are made in bulk, and a plate uses 6 cups of potatoes.

== Spice mix ==

Mix the @cayenne pepper{4%cup}, @smoked paprika{4%cup}, @red chile flakes{2%cup}, @chile powder{2%cup}, @ground cumin{1%cup}, @light brown sugar{1%cup}, @black pepper{1/2%cup}, @garlic powder{1/2%cup}, @onion powder{1/2%cup} and @kosher salt{1/2%cup} in a bowl.

== Hot oil ==

Put 1 cup of the spice mix and the @blended oil{4%cup} in a #sauté pan{} over medium heat. Cook ~{15%minutes} until fragrant, then let cool and keep in an airtight container.

== Ranch ==

Whisk the @mayonnaise{16%cup}, @buttermilk{12%cup}, @sour cream{5%lb}, @parsley{2%cup}(chopped), @kosher salt{1/2%cup}, @garlic powder{1/4%cup}, @onion powder{1/4%cup}, @black pepper{3%tbsp} and @rosemary{2%tbsp}(chopped) together. Keep covered in the fridge.

== Salt-roasted potatoes ==

Heat the oven to 350°F.

Spread the @red potatoes{50%lb} on #sheet trays{} and season with the @kosher salt{5%lb}. Roast ~{30%minutes} until a fork goes in easily.

Cool ~{5%minutes}, then, wearing gloves, crack each potato open while it is still warm. Let cool completely.

== Herb mix ==

Mix the @parsley{1/4%cup}(chopped) and @rosemary{1/4%cup}(chopped).

== To serve ==

Warm 3 oz of the hot oil in a #small saucepan{} over low heat.

Heat @neutral oil{}(for frying) in a #deep fryer{}. Fry 6 cups of the cracked potatoes until golden and crisp.

Toss the potatoes in a bowl with @kosher salt{}, some of the herb mix and the warm hot oil. Pile into a serving bowl, drizzle with ranch and finish with more herb mix.
